<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net">
  <diagram name="Acceptance Criteria — Increment 6" id="ac-increment-6">
    <mxGraphModel dx="0" dy="0" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="13700" pageHeight="900" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
<mxCell id="inc6-crowd-move-stories-2" value="Crowd Move Stories" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="20" width="1610" height="519" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-move-crowd-with-relative-positioning-3" value="Move Crowd with Relative Positioning" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="125.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-move-crowd-with-relative-positioning-ac1-4" value="1. WHEN the GM selects Move Crowd with Relative Positioning from the Context Menu on a spawned crowd member and designates a destination THEN every spawned Roster Entry in the target crowd receives a Movement Execution command AND each member&apos;s destination is its current position plus the same offset vector from the GM&apos;s pick point to the destination AND all members begin moving simultaneously" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="35" y="110" width="300" height="114" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-move-crowd-with-relative-positioning-ac2-5" value="2. WHEN all Movement Execution commands complete THEN all crowd members are at their new positions, each displaced by the same delta AND the Group Formation — the relative offsets between members — is unchanged" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="35" y="234" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-move-crowd-with-relative-positioning-ac3-6" value="3. WHEN the GM triggers Relative Positioning on a crowd that has at least one unspawned member THEN only spawned members receive move commands BUT no error is raised for the unspawned members; they are silently excluded" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="35" y="316" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-move-crowd-with-relative-positioning-ac4-7" value="4. WHEN the destination is the same as the crowd&apos;s current center point THEN move commands are issued with zero offset BUT no error is raised and no member position changes" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="35" y="398" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-move-crowd-with-relative-positioning-ac5-8" value="5. WHEN a Movement Execution command for one member fails mid-move THEN the system reports which member failed BUT commands already issued to other members are not rolled back" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="35" y="466" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-move-crowd-with-optimal-spread-positioning-9" value="Move Crowd with Optimal Spread Positioning" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="445.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-move-crowd-with-optimal-spread-positioning-ac1-10" value="1. WHEN the GM selects Move Crowd with Optimal Spread Positioning from the Context Menu on a spawned crowd member and designates a destination THEN the system computes a set of spread destination slots around the destination center, one per spawned member AND each member is assigned a unique slot that minimizes its individual travel distance AND each member receives a Movement Execution command to its assigned slot" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="355" y="110" width="300" height="114" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-move-crowd-with-optimal-spread-positioning-ac2-11" value="2. WHEN all Movement Execution commands complete THEN the crowd occupies an evenly distributed spread arrangement at the destination AND no two members share the same slot position" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="355" y="234" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-move-crowd-with-optimal-spread-positioning-ac3-12" value="3. WHEN the crowd has only one spawned member THEN that member&apos;s destination slot is the designated destination point itself AND the move completes normally" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="355" y="302" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-move-crowd-with-optimal-spread-positioning-ac4-13" value="4. WHEN the destination area is partially obstructed THEN spread slots in unobstructed areas are assigned first AND members assigned to obstructed slots receive their nearest unobstructed alternative" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="355" y="370" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-move-crowd-with-optimal-spread-positioning-ac5-14" value="5. WHEN the crowd is a Gang Mode group and the GM triggers Optimal Spread Positioning THEN spread positioning is applied to all spawned gang members as normal AND post-move facing alignment uses Gang Leader Facing rather than Facing Destination" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="355" y="452" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-maintain-group-formation-during-crowd-move-15" value="Maintain Group Formation during Crowd Move" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="765.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-maintain-group-formation-during-crowd-move-ac1-16" value="1. WHEN a Crowd Move with Relative Positioning completes THEN the relative offset from each member to every other member is the same after the move as before AND no member has drifted from its expected position relative to its neighbors" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="675" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-maintain-group-formation-during-crowd-move-ac2-17" value="2. WHEN a Crowd Move with Relative Positioning is issued for a crowd whose members have different current positions THEN the Group Formation offsets are captured from the actual positions at move start AND each member&apos;s destination preserves its pre-move offset from the formation center" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="675" y="192" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-maintain-group-formation-during-crowd-move-ac3-18" value="3. WHEN a member&apos;s position cannot be read before the move begins THEN the system reports the missing position data BUT the move is not issued until all member positions are resolved" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="675" y="288" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-maintain-group-formation-during-crowd-move-ac4-19" value="4. WHEN formation is checked after a crowd move using Relative Positioning THEN the pairwise distances between all members match the pairwise distances recorded at move start within the positional tolerance of the movement system BUT the absolute positions are all offset by the move delta" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="675" y="356" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-turn-characters-to-face-destination-20" value="Turn Characters to Face Destination" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1085.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-turn-characters-to-face-destination-ac1-21" value="1. WHEN a Crowd Move completes and the crowd is not an active Gang Mode group THEN a facing command is issued to every moved member pointing toward the movement destination center AND each member&apos;s orientation is updated to face the destination" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="995" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-turn-characters-to-face-destination-ac2-22" value="2. WHEN a Crowd Move completes and the crowd is an active Gang Mode group THEN Gang Leader Facing is applied instead of Facing Destination BUT no facing-destination command is issued" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="995" y="192" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-turn-characters-to-face-destination-ac3-23" value="3. WHEN the destination and a member&apos;s new position are at the same point THEN no facing command is issued for that member BUT all other members receive facing commands normally" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="995" y="260" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-turn-characters-to-face-destination-ac4-24" value="4. WHEN facing commands are issued after a move THEN facing updates are applied before the Crowd Move operation is considered complete AND the Desktop Overlay character overlays reflect the updated orientations" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="995" y="328" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-turn-characters-to-face-destination-ac5-25" value="5. WHEN a facing command for one member fails THEN the failure is reported BUT facing commands for all other members are still applied" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="995" y="410" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-align-character-facing-with-gang-leader-26" value="Align Character Facing with Gang Leader" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1405.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-align-character-facing-with-gang-leader-ac1-27" value="1. WHEN the GM triggers Align Character Facing with Gang Leader for an active Gang Mode group THEN the system reads the current facing vector of the Gang Leader from game memory AND a facing command aligned to that vector is issued to every other spawned gang member" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1315" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-align-character-facing-with-gang-leader-ac2-28" value="2. WHEN Gang Leader Facing is applied during a Crowd Move completion THEN all gang members are oriented to match the Gang Leader&apos;s facing direction AND no facing-destination command is issued" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1315" y="206" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-align-character-facing-with-gang-leader-ac3-29" value="3. WHEN the Gang Leader is not spawned at the time of alignment THEN the system reports that the Gang Leader facing cannot be read BUT no facing commands are issued to any member" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1315" y="288" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-align-character-facing-with-gang-leader-ac4-30" value="4. WHEN a gang member is not spawned at the time of alignment THEN that member is skipped AND all other spawned gang members receive the facing command" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1315" y="356" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-align-character-facing-with-gang-leader-ac5-31" value="5. WHEN Gang Mode is not active for the crowd THEN Gang Leader Facing alignment is not available BUT Facing Destination is applied at crowd move completion" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1315" y="424" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-attack-configuration-stories-32" value="Attack Configuration Stories" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1660" y="20" width="4490" height="505" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-select-attacking-character-33" value="Select Attacking Character" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1765.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-select-attacking-character-ac1-34" value="1. WHEN the GM opens an Attack Configuration by activating an attack ability from the Context Menu on a spawned character THEN the Attack Configuration panel opens AND the activated character is pre-assigned as the Attacker in the Combatant Selectors region AND the character&apos;s Combat State is set to attacker role" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1675" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-select-attacking-character-ac2-35" value="2. WHEN the GM selects a different character as the Attacker via the Select Attacker action THEN the Combatant Selectors region updates to show the newly selected character as the Attacker AND the previous attacker&apos;s Combat State is reset to neutral AND the new attacker&apos;s Combat State is set to attacker role" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1675" y="206" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-select-attacking-character-ac3-36" value="3. WHEN the GM attempts to select a character as Attacker who is already listed as a Defender THEN the selection is rejected with feedback BUT the existing Attacker assignment is unchanged" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1675" y="302" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-select-attacking-character-ac4-37" value="4. WHEN the GM attempts to select an unspawned character as Attacker THEN the selection is rejected with feedback BUT the existing Attacker assignment is unchanged" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1675" y="370" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-activate-attack-ability-38" value="Activate Attack Ability" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2085.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-activate-attack-ability-ac1-39" value="1. WHEN the GM activates an attack ability on a spawned character from the Context Menu on the Desktop THEN the application transitions to the Attack Configuration panel AND the activating character is assigned as the Attacker AND the Attack Configuration panel displays with the Combatant Selectors region and the Attack Parameters region visible" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1995" y="110" width="300" height="100" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-activate-attack-ability-ac2-40" value="2. WHEN the GM activates an attack ability from the Context Menu on a character with no attack ability defined THEN no Attack Configuration opens AND feedback is shown indicating no attack ability is available" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1995" y="220" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-activate-attack-ability-ac3-41" value="3. WHEN the Attack Configuration panel is open THEN the Attacker&apos;s non-attack abilities are locked AND the Confirm button is disabled until at least one Defender is added" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1995" y="302" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-activate-attack-ability-ac4-42" value="4. WHEN the GM cancels from the Attack Configuration panel THEN the panel closes and the application returns to the Desktop AND the Attacker&apos;s Combat State is reset to neutral AND all Non-Attack Ability Lock suppressions are released" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1995" y="370" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-select-defender-targets-43" value="Select Defender Targets" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2405.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-select-defender-targets-ac1-44" value="1. WHEN the GM clicks Add Defender in the Combatant Selectors region and selects a spawned character THEN the selected character is added as a Defender in the list AND an Attacker-Defender Pair record is created for this defender with default parameter values AND the defender&apos;s Combat State is set to defender role" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2315" y="110" width="300" height="100" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-select-defender-targets-ac2-45" value="2. WHEN the GM adds a second and subsequent Defenders THEN each new character is appended to the Combatant Selectors list AND each receives its own Attacker-Defender Pair with independent parameters" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2315" y="220" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-select-defender-targets-ac3-46" value="3. WHEN the GM attempts to add a character that is already the Attacker as a Defender THEN the addition is rejected with feedback BUT existing defenders are unchanged" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2315" y="302" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-select-defender-targets-ac4-47" value="4. WHEN the GM attempts to add an unspawned character as a Defender THEN the addition is rejected BUT the existing defender list is unchanged" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2315" y="370" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-select-defender-targets-ac5-48" value="5. WHEN the GM removes a Defender using Remove Defender THEN the defender is removed from the Combatant Selectors list AND their Attacker-Defender Pair record is deleted AND their Combat State is reset to neutral" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2315" y="438" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-confirm-attack-targets-49" value="Confirm Attack Targets" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2725.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-confirm-attack-targets-ac1-50" value="1. WHEN the GM clicks Confirm Targets in the Combatant Selectors region with one Attacker and at least one Defender selected THEN the combatant list is locked AND the Attack Parameters region becomes fully editable AND each Attacker-Defender Pair is confirmed with default values" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2635" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-confirm-attack-targets-ac2-51" value="2. WHEN Confirm Targets is triggered with no Defender in the list THEN the confirmation is rejected AND feedback is displayed indicating at least one defender is required BUT the Combatant Selectors list is unchanged" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2635" y="206" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-confirm-attack-targets-ac3-52" value="3. WHEN Confirm Targets is triggered with no Attacker assigned THEN the confirmation is rejected AND feedback is displayed BUT no lock-in occurs" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2635" y="288" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-confirm-attack-targets-ac4-53" value="4. WHEN the combatant list is locked after Confirm Targets THEN the Add Defender and Remove Defender actions are disabled AND the Combat State of all combatants reflects their confirmed roles" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2635" y="356" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-configure-attack-for-attacker-defender-pair-54" value="Configure Attack for Attacker-Defender Pair" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3045.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-configure-attack-for-attacker-defender-pair-ac1-55" value="1. WHEN the GM edits Attack Effect, Knockback Distance, Attack Result, and Attack Mode for a specific Attacker-Defender Pair in the Attack Parameters region THEN each parameter is stored independently on that pair&apos;s record AND changes to one pair&apos;s parameters do not affect any other pair" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2955" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-configure-attack-for-attacker-defender-pair-ac2-56" value="2. WHEN the GM selects a different Attack Effect for a pair THEN the dropdown updates to show the selected effect AND the pair record stores the new value immediately" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2955" y="206" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-configure-attack-for-attacker-defender-pair-ac3-57" value="3. WHEN the GM enters a negative value for Knockback Distance THEN the value is rejected and the field reverts to zero AND feedback is shown" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2955" y="274" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-configure-attack-for-attacker-defender-pair-ac4-58" value="4. WHEN the Attack Configuration has multiple Defenders THEN each Attacker-Defender Pair shows its independently configured parameters AND selecting a different row in the Combatant Selectors list updates the Attack Parameters region to reflect that pair&apos;s values" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2955" y="342" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-configure-attack-for-attacker-defender-pair-ac5-59" value="5. WHEN the GM leaves all parameters at default and confirms THEN default values (Miss, zero knockback, Stunned, Attack mode) are used for execution" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2955" y="438" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-set-attack-effect-stunned-unconscious-dying-dead-60" value="Set Attack Effect (Stunned, Unconscious, Dying, Dead)" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3365.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-set-attack-effect-stunned-unconscious-dying-dead-ac1-61" value="1. WHEN the GM selects Stunned, Unconscious, Dying, or Dead from the Attack Effect dropdown for a pair THEN the Attack Effect for that Attacker-Defender Pair is set to the chosen value AND the corresponding On-Hit Animation will be selected at execution time" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3275" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-set-attack-effect-stunned-unconscious-dying-dead-ac2-62" value="2. WHEN the Attack Result for the pair is Hit and Confirm is pressed THEN the Status Effect matching the Attack Effect is applied to the Defender during execution AND the Attack State Indicator on the defender&apos;s Character Overlay is updated" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3275" y="206" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-set-attack-effect-stunned-unconscious-dying-dead-ac3-63" value="3. WHEN the Attack Result for the pair is Miss THEN no Status Effect is applied regardless of the Attack Effect setting BUT the Attack Effect value is preserved in the pair configuration" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3275" y="288" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-set-attack-effect-stunned-unconscious-dying-dead-ac4-64" value="4. WHEN no Attack Effect is selected (field left blank) THEN Confirm is blocked with feedback indicating Attack Effect is required BUT all other pair parameters are unchanged" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3275" y="356" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-set-knockback-distance-65" value="Set Knockback Distance" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3685.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-set-knockback-distance-ac1-66" value="1. WHEN the GM enters a positive integer in the Knockback Distance field for a pair THEN Knockback Distance for that Attacker-Defender Pair is updated AND a Knockback Movement command of that distance will be issued during execution when Attack Result is Hit" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3595" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-set-knockback-distance-ac2-67" value="2. WHEN the GM enters zero in the Knockback Distance field THEN no Knockback Movement is applied during execution for that pair AND the field accepts zero as a valid value" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3595" y="206" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-set-knockback-distance-ac3-68" value="3. WHEN Knockback Distance is greater than zero and Attack Result is Hit THEN a Collision Ray is fired along the knockback vector before the displacement is applied AND if Knockback Obstruction is detected, the defender is moved only to the obstruction point AND the Attack State Indicator reflects the applied Status Effect regardless of clipped distance" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3595" y="274" width="300" height="100" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-set-knockback-distance-ac4-69" value="4. WHEN the GM enters a non-numeric value in the Knockback Distance field THEN the value is rejected and the field is cleared AND feedback is shown" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3595" y="384" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-set-attack-result-hit-or-miss-70" value="Set Attack Result (Hit or Miss)" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4005.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-set-attack-result-hit-or-miss-ac1-71" value="1. WHEN the GM selects Hit from the Attack Result dropdown for a pair THEN the pair&apos;s Attack Result is set to Hit AND On-Hit Animation, Knockback Movement, and Status Effect application are all enabled for this pair&apos;s execution" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3915" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-set-attack-result-hit-or-miss-ac2-72" value="2. WHEN the GM selects Miss from the Attack Result dropdown for a pair THEN the pair&apos;s Attack Result is set to Miss AND On-Hit Animation, Knockback Movement, and Status Effect are all skipped for this pair during execution BUT Attack Animation on the Attacker still plays" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3915" y="192" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-set-attack-result-hit-or-miss-ac3-73" value="3. WHEN a multi-defender configuration has some pairs set to Hit and others to Miss THEN each pair&apos;s execution is independent AND only Hit pairs apply effects; Miss pairs skip effects without affecting other pairs" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3915" y="288" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-set-attack-result-hit-or-miss-ac4-74" value="4. WHEN no Attack Result is selected THEN Confirm is blocked with feedback" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3915" y="370" width="300" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-set-attack-mode-attack-or-defend-75" value="Set Attack Mode (Attack or Defend)" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4325.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-set-attack-mode-attack-or-defend-ac1-76" value="1. WHEN the GM selects Attack from the Attack Mode dropdown THEN the Attack Configuration&apos;s Attack Mode is set to Attack AND the mode is recorded in the confirmed configuration for HCS reporting" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4235" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-set-attack-mode-attack-or-defend-ac2-77" value="2. WHEN the GM selects Defend from the Attack Mode dropdown THEN the Attack Configuration&apos;s Attack Mode is set to Defend AND the mode is recorded accordingly" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4235" y="192" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-set-attack-mode-attack-or-defend-ac3-78" value="3. WHEN the Attack Configuration is confirmed with Attack Mode set to Defend THEN the execution proceeds identically to Attack mode (animations and effects are applied) AND the Defend mode is passed to the HCS event pipeline for turn-state tracking" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4235" y="260" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-set-attack-mode-attack-or-defend-ac4-79" value="4. WHEN no Attack Mode is selected THEN a default of Attack is used AND no confirmation block occurs" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4235" y="342" width="300" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-designate-center-target-for-area-attack-80" value="Designate Center Target for Area Attack" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4645.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-designate-center-target-for-area-attack-ac1-81" value="1. WHEN the GM checks the Area Center option in the Attack Parameters region THEN the Attack Configuration enters area-attack mode AND the GM is prompted to designate the center target in the COH game view using the Area Attack Pop-Up Menu" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4555" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-designate-center-target-for-area-attack-ac2-82" value="2. WHEN the GM designates a center target via the Area Attack Pop-Up Menu THEN the Area Center character name is populated in the Attack Parameters region AND all spawned characters within the area radius of the Area Center are automatically added as Defenders" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4555" y="192" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-designate-center-target-for-area-attack-ac3-83" value="3. WHEN the Area Attack Pop-Up Menu is not deployed THEN area center designation is blocked AND feedback is displayed indicating the menu must be loaded first BUT the Attack Configuration remains open" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4555" y="288" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-designate-center-target-for-area-attack-ac4-84" value="4. WHEN no characters are within the area radius of the designated Area Center THEN no Defenders are added automatically AND feedback indicates the area is empty BUT the Area Center designation is preserved" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4555" y="370" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-designate-center-target-for-area-attack-ac5-85" value="5. WHEN the GM unchecks the Area Center option THEN all automatically added Defenders are removed from the list AND the configuration reverts to single-target mode" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4555" y="452" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-execute-ranged-area-attack-86" value="Execute Ranged Area Attack" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4965.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-execute-ranged-area-attack-ac1-87" value="1. WHEN the GM confirms an Area Attack with an Area Center designated and Defenders populated THEN Line-of-Sight is calculated from the Attacker to each Defender AND only Defenders with a clear Line-of-Sight are included in Combat Execution" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4875" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-execute-ranged-area-attack-ac2-88" value="2. WHEN Line-of-Sight to a Defender is blocked THEN that Defender is excluded from the attack AND the GM is shown which defenders were excluded BUT the attack proceeds for all defenders with clear LOS" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4875" y="192" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-execute-ranged-area-attack-ac3-89" value="3. WHEN all Defenders have blocked Line-of-Sight THEN no execution occurs AND feedback is displayed indicating no valid targets" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4875" y="274" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-execute-ranged-area-attack-ac4-90" value="4. WHEN execution proceeds with valid area targets THEN Attack Animation plays on the Attacker once AND On-Hit Animation, Knockback Movement, and Status Effect are applied per pair to each included Defender" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4875" y="342" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-execute-sweep-attack-across-multiple-targets-91" value="Execute Sweep Attack across Multiple Targets" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5285.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-execute-sweep-attack-across-multiple-targets-ac1-92" value="1. WHEN the GM confirms a Sweep Attack with multiple Defenders THEN execution begins with the first Attacker-Defender Pair in the Combatant Selectors list AND Attack Animation plays on the Attacker AND after animation completion, the Defender&apos;s On-Hit Animation, Knockback Movement, and Status Effect are applied per the pair&apos;s configuration AND then execution advances to the next pair in sequence" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5195" y="110" width="300" height="114" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-execute-sweep-attack-across-multiple-targets-ac2-93" value="2. WHEN all Attacker-Defender Pairs have been resolved THEN execution is complete AND all Attack State Indicators are updated AND the Attack Configuration closes and the Desktop screen is shown" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5195" y="234" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-execute-sweep-attack-across-multiple-targets-ac3-94" value="3. WHEN a pair&apos;s Attack Result is Miss THEN the Attack Animation still plays AND no On-Hit Animation, Knockback, or Status Effect is applied for that pair AND execution advances to the next pair" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5195" y="316" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-execute-sweep-attack-across-multiple-targets-ac4-95" value="4. WHEN execution is aborted mid-sweep THEN no further pairs are resolved AND Combat State of all combatants is reset AND Attack State Indicators reflect any effects already applied before the abort" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5195" y="384" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-assign-auto-fire-shots-per-target-96" value="Assign Auto-Fire Shots per Target" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5605.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-assign-auto-fire-shots-per-target-ac1-97" value="1. WHEN the GM enters a total shot count in the Auto-Fire Shots per Target field for a Sweep Attack THEN shots are distributed across all Defenders proportionally AND each Attacker-Defender Pair is assigned an integer shot count" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5515" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-assign-auto-fire-shots-per-target-ac2-98" value="2. WHEN total shots do not divide evenly across Defenders THEN the remainder shots are allocated starting from the first defender in the list AND all shots are distributed with none omitted" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5515" y="192" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-assign-auto-fire-shots-per-target-ac3-99" value="3. WHEN total shot count is zero or blank THEN auto-fire distribution is skipped AND each pair defaults to a single exchange" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5515" y="274" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-assign-auto-fire-shots-per-target-ac4-100" value="4. WHEN auto-fire assigns more than one shot to a pair THEN the Attack Animation and effect sequence is repeated for each shot on that pair AND the effect accumulates or is overwritten per the configured Attack Effect for the pair" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5515" y="342" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-spread-attack-across-crowd-101" value="Spread Attack across Crowd" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5925.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-spread-attack-across-crowd-ac1-102" value="1. WHEN the GM triggers Spread Attack across Crowd and designates an Area Center within the target crowd THEN all spawned members of the crowd within the area radius are added as Defenders automatically AND an Attacker-Defender Pair is created for each with the same default parameters" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5835" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-spread-attack-across-crowd-ac2-103" value="2. WHEN multiple crowds have members within range THEN all in-range members from all crowds are included as Defenders" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5835" y="206" width="300" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-spread-attack-across-crowd-ac3-104" value="3. WHEN no crowd members are within range of the Area Center THEN no Defenders are added AND feedback indicates the area contains no crowd members BUT the Attack Configuration remains open" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5835" y="266" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-combat-execution-stories-105" value="Combat Execution Stories" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6180" y="20" width="3210" height="491" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-play-attack-animation-on-attacker-106" value="Play Attack Animation on Attacker" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6285.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-play-attack-animation-on-attacker-ac1-107" value="1. WHEN Combat Execution begins a pair resolution THEN the Attack Animation associated with the Attacker&apos;s attack ability is played AND execution waits for the animation to complete before proceeding to the defender step" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6195" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-play-attack-animation-on-attacker-ac2-108" value="2. WHEN the Attack Animation completes THEN execution advances to the On-Hit Animation step for the paired Defender" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6195" y="192" width="300" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-play-attack-animation-on-attacker-ac3-109" value="3. WHEN the Attacker has no attack animation configured THEN the animation step is skipped AND execution advances to the defender step immediately" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6195" y="252" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-play-attack-animation-on-attacker-ac4-110" value="4. WHEN the Attacker is not spawned at execution time THEN the animation is skipped and execution reports the attacker unavailable BUT the remaining pair resolutions are aborted" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6195" y="320" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-play-on-hit-animation-on-defender-111" value="Play On-Hit Animation on Defender" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6605.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-play-on-hit-animation-on-defender-ac1-112" value="1. WHEN the pair&apos;s Attack Result is Hit THEN the On-Hit Animation corresponding to the pair&apos;s Attack Effect is played on the Defender AND execution waits for the animation to complete before proceeding to Knockback Movement" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6515" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-play-on-hit-animation-on-defender-ac2-113" value="2. WHEN the pair&apos;s Attack Result is Miss THEN no On-Hit Animation is played for the Defender AND execution advances directly to the next pair" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6515" y="192" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-play-on-hit-animation-on-defender-ac3-114" value="3. WHEN the Defender has no on-hit animation configured for the given Attack Effect THEN the animation step is skipped AND Knockback Movement and Status Effect application still proceed" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6515" y="260" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-play-on-hit-animation-on-defender-ac4-115" value="4. WHEN the Defender is not spawned at execution time THEN the on-hit step is skipped and a warning is recorded AND execution advances to the next pair" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6515" y="328" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-apply-knockback-movement-to-defender-116" value="Apply Knockback Movement to Defender" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6925.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-apply-knockback-movement-to-defender-ac1-117" value="1. WHEN the pair&apos;s Attack Result is Hit and Knockback Distance is greater than zero THEN a Collision Ray is fired from the Defender&apos;s position along the knockback vector AND the knockback destination is set to the full Knockback Distance if the ray is clear AND a Movement Execution command displaces the Defender to the computed destination" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6835" y="110" width="300" height="100" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-apply-knockback-movement-to-defender-ac2-118" value="2. WHEN the Collision Ray detects Knockback Obstruction THEN the knockback destination is set to the obstruction point AND the Defender is moved only to the obstruction edge AND the Attack State Indicator still reflects the Status Effect" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6835" y="220" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-apply-knockback-movement-to-defender-ac3-119" value="3. WHEN Knockback Distance is zero THEN no Collision Ray is fired and no movement command is issued AND Status Effect application proceeds normally" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6835" y="302" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-apply-knockback-movement-to-defender-ac4-120" value="4. WHEN the pair&apos;s Attack Result is Miss THEN no knockback command is issued BUT the pair&apos;s Knockback Distance setting is preserved for reference" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6835" y="370" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-apply-status-effect-to-defender-stunned-unconscious-dying-dead-121" value="Apply Status Effect to Defender (Stunned, Unconscious, Dying, Dead)" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7245.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-apply-status-effect-to-defender-stunned-unconscious-dying-dead-ac1-122" value="1. WHEN the pair&apos;s Attack Result is Hit THEN the Status Effect corresponding to the pair&apos;s Attack Effect is applied to the Defender&apos;s Combat State AND the Attack State Indicator on the Defender&apos;s Character Overlay is updated to show the effect name" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7155" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-apply-status-effect-to-defender-stunned-unconscious-dying-dead-ac2-123" value="2. WHEN a Defender already has an active Status Effect from a prior attack in the same session THEN the new Status Effect replaces the prior one AND the Attack State Indicator is updated to reflect the new effect" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7155" y="192" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-apply-status-effect-to-defender-stunned-unconscious-dying-dead-ac3-124" value="3. WHEN the pair&apos;s Attack Result is Miss THEN no Status Effect is applied AND any existing Status Effect on the Defender from a prior attack is unchanged" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7155" y="274" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-apply-status-effect-to-defender-stunned-unconscious-dying-dead-ac4-125" value="4. WHEN a Dead Status Effect is applied THEN the Defender&apos;s Combat State is marked Dead AND all further combat actions targeting the Dead Defender are blocked in the UI BUT the Defender remains in the Roster and on the Desktop Overlay unless explicitly removed by the GM" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7155" y="342" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-update-character-attack-state-indicators-126" value="Update Character Attack State Indicators" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7565.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-update-character-attack-state-indicators-ac1-127" value="1. WHEN a Status Effect is applied to a Defender during execution THEN the Attack State Indicator on the Defender&apos;s Character Overlay is updated immediately to show the effect label AND the indicator is visible on the Desktop Overlay" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7475" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-update-character-attack-state-indicators-ac2-128" value="2. WHEN a character&apos;s Combat State shows an active attacker role THEN the Attack State Indicator shows an attacker designation AND the indicator persists until Combat State is reset" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7475" y="192" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-update-character-attack-state-indicators-ac3-129" value="3. WHEN Combat State is reset for a character THEN the Attack State Indicator on that character&apos;s Character Overlay is cleared AND the overlay returns to its standard non-combat display" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7475" y="260" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-update-character-attack-state-indicators-ac4-130" value="4. WHEN Combat Execution completes all pairs THEN all Attack State Indicators reflect the final applied Status Effects before the Attack Configuration closes" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7475" y="328" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-cancel-active-attack-131" value="Cancel Active Attack" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7885.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-cancel-active-attack-ac1-132" value="1. WHEN the GM clicks Cancel in the Attack Configuration panel before clicking Confirm THEN the Attack Configuration panel closes AND the application returns to the Desktop AND the Combat State of the Attacker and all Defenders is reset to neutral AND all Non-Attack Ability Lock suppressions are released" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7795" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-cancel-active-attack-ac2-133" value="2. WHEN Cancel is clicked after parameters are partially configured THEN all unsaved parameters are discarded AND no effects are applied to any character" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7795" y="206" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-cancel-active-attack-ac3-134" value="3. WHEN Cancel is triggered via keyboard shortcut THEN the same result as clicking Cancel applies" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7795" y="274" width="300" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-cancel-active-attack-ac4-135" value="4. WHEN the GM closes the Attack Configuration panel without using Cancel or Confirm THEN the behavior is equivalent to Cancel: Combat State resets and the Desktop is shown" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7795" y="334" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-abort-attack-in-progress-136" value="Abort Attack in Progress" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8205.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-abort-attack-in-progress-ac1-137" value="1. WHEN the GM clicks Abort during Combat Execution THEN the current animation (if running) completes AND no further Attacker-Defender Pairs are resolved AND execution stops" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8115" y="110" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-abort-attack-in-progress-ac2-138" value="2. WHEN execution stops after an Abort THEN the Combat State of all Combatants is reset to neutral AND Attack State Indicators reflect any Status Effects applied before the abort point AND the Attack Configuration panel closes and the Desktop is shown" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8115" y="178" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-abort-attack-in-progress-ac3-139" value="3. WHEN Abort is triggered before any pair has been resolved THEN no effects have been applied AND the reset leaves all characters in their pre-configuration state" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8115" y="260" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-abort-attack-in-progress-ac4-140" value="4. WHEN Abort is triggered for a Sweep Attack mid-sequence THEN pairs already resolved retain their applied effects AND unresolved pairs produce no effects" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8115" y="328" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-abort-attack-in-progress-ac5-141" value="5. WHEN Abort is not available (e.g. before Confirm is clicked) THEN the Abort button is disabled AND Cancel is the applicable exit" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8115" y="396" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-reset-character-combat-state-142" value="Reset Character Combat State" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8525.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-reset-character-combat-state-ac1-143" value="1. WHEN the GM triggers Reset Character Combat State on a specific character THEN that character&apos;s Combat State is set to neutral AND all active Status Effects are cleared from the Combat State record AND the Attack State Indicator on the character&apos;s Character Overlay is cleared AND any Non-Attack Ability Lock on that character is released" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8435" y="110" width="300" height="100" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-reset-character-combat-state-ac2-144" value="2. WHEN Reset is triggered on a character currently in an active Attack Configuration THEN the reset is blocked AND feedback is displayed indicating the character is in an active configuration BUT the character&apos;s Combat State is unchanged" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8435" y="220" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-reset-character-combat-state-ac3-145" value="3. WHEN Reset is triggered after a completed or aborted attack THEN the character&apos;s Combat State resets normally regardless of prior Status Effect state" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8435" y="302" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-reset-character-combat-state-ac4-146" value="4. WHEN the GM resets a character with a Dead Status Effect THEN the Dead state is cleared from Combat State AND the character becomes eligible for combat again BUT the GM must re-confirm the character&apos;s roster presence before attacking or defending" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8435" y="370" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-disable-non-attack-abilities-during-combat-147" value="Disable Non-Attack Abilities during Combat" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8845.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-disable-non-attack-abilities-during-combat-ac1-148" value="1. WHEN a character is assigned as Attacker or Defender in an Attack Configuration THEN all non-attack Animated Abilities on that character are locked from activation AND any attempt to trigger a non-attack ability is silently blocked while the lock is active" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8755" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-disable-non-attack-abilities-during-combat-ac2-149" value="2. WHEN the Attack Configuration is confirmed and execution begins THEN the Non-Attack Ability Lock remains active on all Combatants throughout execution" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8755" y="206" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-disable-non-attack-abilities-during-combat-ac3-150" value="3. WHEN the Attack Configuration is cancelled, completed, or aborted THEN the Non-Attack Ability Lock is released for all Combatants AND non-attack abilities become available for activation again" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8755" y="274" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-disable-non-attack-abilities-during-combat-ac4-151" value="4. WHEN a character is removed from the Attack Configuration before Confirm THEN their Non-Attack Ability Lock is released immediately upon removal" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8755" y="356" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-track-attacker-and-defender-roles-per-character-152" value="Track Attacker and Defender Roles per Character" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9165.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-track-attacker-and-defender-roles-per-character-ac1-153" value="1. WHEN a character is assigned as Attacker in an Attack Configuration THEN their Combat State shows role = attacker AND the Attack State Indicator shows the attacker designation on the Character Overlay" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9075" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-track-attacker-and-defender-roles-per-character-ac2-154" value="2. WHEN a character is assigned as Defender THEN their Combat State shows role = defender AND the Attack State Indicator shows the defender designation" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9075" y="192" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-track-attacker-and-defender-roles-per-character-ac3-155" value="3. WHEN a character holds both an attacker and defender role assignment simultaneously (invalid state) THEN the second assignment is blocked AND feedback is shown" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9075" y="260" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-track-attacker-and-defender-roles-per-character-ac4-156" value="4. WHEN a character&apos;s role is removed (defender removed, or configuration cancelled) THEN their Combat State role is reset to neutral AND the role indicator on the Character Overlay is cleared" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9075" y="328" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-track-attacker-and-defender-roles-per-character-ac5-157" value="5. WHEN the session has multiple simultaneous Attack Configurations open THEN each character&apos;s Combat State reflects its role in its own configuration independently BUT a character may not hold a role in more than one active configuration at the same time" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9075" y="410" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-combat-geometry-stories-158" value="Combat Geometry Stories" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9420" y="20" width="970" height="455" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-detect-knockback-obstruction-via-collision-ray-159" value="Detect Knockback Obstruction via Collision Ray" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9525.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-detect-knockback-obstruction-via-collision-ray-ac1-160" value="1. WHEN Knockback Distance is greater than zero for a Hit pair THEN a Collision Ray is issued from the Defender&apos;s position along the knockback direction vector, up to Knockback Distance units AND Game Collision Detection returns the first obstruction point (or a clear result)" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9435" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-detect-knockback-obstruction-via-collision-ray-ac2-161" value="2. WHEN Game Collision Detection returns an obstruction THEN Knockback Obstruction is recorded at the obstruction distance AND Knockback Movement is applied only to the obstruction point, not the full Knockback Distance" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9435" y="206" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-detect-knockback-obstruction-via-collision-ray-ac3-162" value="3. WHEN Game Collision Detection returns a clear path THEN Knockback Movement is applied for the full Knockback Distance" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9435" y="288" width="300" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-detect-knockback-obstruction-via-collision-ray-ac4-163" value="4. WHEN the COH game client is not running at query time THEN Game Collision Detection returns a clear-path result as the safe default AND the full Knockback Distance is applied AND a warning is logged that the collision query was unavailable" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9435" y="348" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-calculate-line-of-sight-for-ranged-attack-164" value="Calculate Line-of-Sight for Ranged Attack" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9845.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-calculate-line-of-sight-for-ranged-attack-ac1-165" value="1. WHEN the GM confirms a Ranged Attack THEN a Collision Ray is issued from the Attacker&apos;s position to each Defender&apos;s position AND Game Collision Detection returns a clear or blocked result for each" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9755" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-calculate-line-of-sight-for-ranged-attack-ac2-166" value="2. WHEN Line-of-Sight to a Defender is clear THEN that Defender is included in Combat Execution normally" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9755" y="192" width="300" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-calculate-line-of-sight-for-ranged-attack-ac3-167" value="3. WHEN Line-of-Sight to a Defender is blocked THEN that Defender is excluded from execution AND the GM is shown which defenders were excluded and why BUT other defenders with clear LOS are included" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9755" y="252" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-calculate-line-of-sight-for-ranged-attack-ac4-168" value="4. WHEN all defenders have blocked Line-of-Sight THEN Confirm is blocked AND feedback indicates no valid targets for the ranged attack" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9755" y="334" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-calculate-line-of-sight-for-ranged-attack-ac5-169" value="5. WHEN the COH game client is not running at LOS query time THEN all defenders are treated as clear LOS (safe default) AND a warning is logged" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9755" y="402" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-query-game-collision-detection-via-hookcostume-dll-170" value="Query Game Collision Detection via HookCostume DLL" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10165.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-query-game-collision-detection-via-hookcostume-dll-ac1-171" value="1. WHEN a Collision Ray query is issued by the application THEN the query parameters are passed to the HookCostume DLL via the Game Bridge AND the DLL returns the distance and position of the first obstruction, or a clear-path indicator" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10075" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-query-game-collision-detection-via-hookcostume-dll-ac2-172" value="2. WHEN the Game Bridge is not initialized at query time THEN the query returns a clear-path result as the safe default AND a warning is logged indicating the DLL was unavailable" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10075" y="192" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-query-game-collision-detection-via-hookcostume-dll-ac3-173" value="3. WHEN a query is issued with zero maximum distance THEN the DLL immediately returns a clear-path result AND no obstruction processing is performed" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10075" y="260" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-query-game-collision-detection-via-hookcostume-dll-ac4-174" value="4. WHEN the DLL returns an error response THEN the application logs the error AND a clear-path result is used as the fallback BUT the invoking operation (LOS check or knockback) proceeds with the fallback" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10075" y="328" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-hcs-integration-stories-175" value="HCS Integration Stories" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10420" y="20" width="3210" height="395" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-start-hcs-file-watcher-integration-176" value="Start HCS File Watcher Integration" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10525.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-start-hcs-file-watcher-integration-ac1-177" value="1. WHEN the GM triggers Start HCS File Watcher Integration THEN the HCS File Watcher begins monitoring the designated HCS output directory for new or updated Info Files AND the HCS integration status indicator shows active" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10435" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-start-hcs-file-watcher-integration-ac2-178" value="2. WHEN the Game Bridge is not initialized at start time THEN the start is blocked AND feedback is displayed indicating the game bridge must be initialized first BUT the HCS integration state is not changed" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10435" y="192" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-start-hcs-file-watcher-integration-ac3-179" value="3. WHEN the HCS output directory does not exist THEN the start is blocked AND feedback indicates the directory cannot be found BUT the HCS File Watcher is not activated" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10435" y="274" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-start-hcs-file-watcher-integration-ac4-180" value="4. WHEN HCS Integration is already active THEN a second Start request is a no-op AND no duplicate watcher is created" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10435" y="342" width="300" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-read-on-deck-combatants-from-info-file-181" value="Read On-Deck Combatants from Info File" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10845.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-read-on-deck-combatants-from-info-file-ac1-182" value="1. WHEN a new Info File arrives and contains an on-deck combatants list THEN the HCS File Watcher reads the list AND each named character is matched to a Roster Entry AND the matched Character Overlays are highlighted to indicate upcoming-turn status" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10755" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-read-on-deck-combatants-from-info-file-ac2-183" value="2. WHEN a named character in the on-deck list does not match any Roster Entry THEN that character is skipped AND a warning is logged BUT other matched characters are processed normally" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10755" y="206" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-read-on-deck-combatants-from-info-file-ac3-184" value="3. WHEN the on-deck list is empty THEN no character overlays are highlighted for on-deck status AND no error is raised" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10755" y="274" width="300" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-read-eligible-combatants-from-info-file-185" value="Read Eligible Combatants from Info File" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="11165.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-read-eligible-combatants-from-info-file-ac1-186" value="1. WHEN a new Info File arrives with an eligible combatants list THEN each named character is matched to a Roster Entry AND eligible status is reflected in the HVT UI for matched characters" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="11075" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-read-eligible-combatants-from-info-file-ac2-187" value="2. WHEN a character in the eligible list does not match any Roster Entry THEN the character is skipped with a warning BUT other eligible characters are processed" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="11075" y="192" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-read-eligible-combatants-from-info-file-ac3-188" value="3. WHEN the eligible list is empty THEN no characters are marked eligible AND the UI reflects no eligible combatants for the current phase" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="11075" y="260" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-read-active-character-from-info-file-189" value="Read Active Character from Info File" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="11485.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-read-active-character-from-info-file-ac1-190" value="1. WHEN a new Info File arrives with an active character designation THEN the HCS File Watcher reads the active character name AND matches it to a Roster Entry AND the HVT Active Character selection is synchronized to the matched Roster Entry" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="11395" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-read-active-character-from-info-file-ac2-191" value="2. WHEN the designated Active Character (HCS) does not match any Roster Entry THEN no roster selection change is made AND a warning is logged with the unmatched character name" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="11395" y="192" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-read-active-character-from-info-file-ac3-192" value="3. WHEN the active character designation is absent from the Info File THEN the current HVT Active Character selection is unchanged AND no error is raised" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="11395" y="260" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-read-chronometer-turn-state-from-info-file-193" value="Read Chronometer Turn State from Info File" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="11805.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-read-chronometer-turn-state-from-info-file-ac1-194" value="1. WHEN a new Info File arrives with chronometer turn state data THEN each named character&apos;s phase is read AND each character&apos;s Combat State is updated to reflect their current HCS phase" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="11715" y="110" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-read-chronometer-turn-state-from-info-file-ac2-195" value="2. WHEN a character&apos;s HCS phase changes to held THEN their Combat State is updated to reflect the held state AND the Attack State Indicator is updated accordingly" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="11715" y="178" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-read-chronometer-turn-state-from-info-file-ac3-196" value="3. WHEN a character listed in the Chronometer Turn State is not in the Roster THEN that character is skipped AND a warning is logged" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="11715" y="246" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-process-attack-result-events-from-hcs-197" value="Process Attack Result Events from HCS" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="12125.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-process-attack-result-events-from-hcs-ac1-198" value="1. WHEN the HCS File Watcher reads an Attack Result Event from an Info File THEN the event payload (attacker, defender(s), Hit or Miss) is dispatched to Combat Execution AND Combat Execution applies effects per the event parameters to the matched Roster Entries" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="12035" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-process-attack-result-events-from-hcs-ac2-199" value="2. WHEN the Attack Result Event payload names characters not in the Roster THEN unmatched characters are skipped AND a warning is logged BUT matched characters receive their effects normally" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="12035" y="206" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-process-attack-result-events-from-hcs-ac3-200" value="3. WHEN the Attack Result Event specifies a Miss THEN no Status Effect, On-Hit Animation, or Knockback is applied AND the Attack Animation on the attacker still plays" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="12035" y="274" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-process-attack-result-events-from-hcs-ac4-201" value="4. WHEN multiple Attack Result Events arrive in the same Info File THEN each event is processed in file order AND each is dispatched independently to Combat Execution" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="12035" y="342" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-process-simple-ability-events-from-hcs-202" value="Process Simple Ability Events from HCS" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="12445.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-process-simple-ability-events-from-hcs-ac1-203" value="1. WHEN the HCS File Watcher reads a Simple Ability Event from an Info File THEN the named ability is triggered on the named character&apos;s Animated Ability playback path" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="12355" y="110" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-process-simple-ability-events-from-hcs-ac2-204" value="2. WHEN the named character is not in the Roster THEN the event is skipped with a warning" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="12355" y="178" width="300" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-process-simple-ability-events-from-hcs-ac3-205" value="3. WHEN the named ability does not exist on the character THEN a warning is logged AND no ability is played BUT other events from the same Info File are still processed" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="12355" y="238" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-process-simple-ability-events-from-hcs-ac4-206" value="4. WHEN the character has a Non-Attack Ability Lock active THEN the Simple Ability Event is blocked from triggering the ability AND a warning is logged indicating the lock prevented playback" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="12355" y="306" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-resolve-held-character-state-from-hcs-207" value="Resolve Held Character State from HCS" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="12765.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-resolve-held-character-state-from-hcs-ac1-208" value="1. WHEN the HCS File Watcher reads a Held Character State entry from an Info File THEN the named character&apos;s Combat State is updated to reflect the held phase AND the Attack State Indicator on the character&apos;s Character Overlay shows the held designation" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="12675" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-resolve-held-character-state-from-hcs-ac2-209" value="2. WHEN the held character is not in the Roster THEN the entry is skipped with a warning" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="12675" y="192" width="300" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-resolve-held-character-state-from-hcs-ac3-210" value="3. WHEN a subsequent Info File no longer lists a character as held THEN the held designation is removed from the character&apos;s Combat State AND the Attack State Indicator is updated to reflect the new phase" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="12675" y="252" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-execute-sweep-results-from-hcs-211" value="Execute Sweep Results from HCS" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="13085.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-execute-sweep-results-from-hcs-ac1-212" value="1. WHEN the HCS File Watcher reads Sweep Results from an Info File THEN the payload is dispatched to the Sweep Attack execution path AND each entry in the payload is treated as an Attacker-Defender Pair to be resolved in sequence" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="12995" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-execute-sweep-results-from-hcs-ac2-213" value="2. WHEN an entry in the Sweep Results lists a defender not in the Roster THEN that entry is skipped AND all other entries are resolved normally" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="12995" y="192" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-execute-sweep-results-from-hcs-ac3-214" value="3. WHEN the sweep execution applies effects to all listed defenders THEN Attack State Indicators are updated for each affected character AND the Attack Configuration is closed after all pairs resolve" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="12995" y="260" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-execute-sweep-results-from-hcs-ac4-215" value="4. WHEN the Sweep Results payload is empty THEN no execution occurs AND a warning is logged" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="12995" y="342" width="300" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-stop-hcs-integration-216" value="Stop HCS Integration" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="13405.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-stop-hcs-integration-ac1-217" value="1. WHEN the GM triggers Stop HCS Integration THEN the HCS File Watcher stops monitoring the output directory AND the HCS integration status indicator shows inactive" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="13315" y="110" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-stop-hcs-integration-ac2-218" value="2. WHEN an Info File is being processed at the time Stop is triggered THEN the current file processing completes AND no further files are read after processing is done" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="13315" y="178" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-stop-hcs-integration-ac3-219" value="3. WHEN HCS Integration is already stopped THEN a Stop request is a no-op AND no error is raised" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="13315" y="246" width="300" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc6-stop-hcs-integration-ac4-220" value="4. WHEN the session ends while HCS Integration is active THEN the HCS File Watcher is stopped automatically AND no further file events are processed" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="13315" y="306" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>